Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.20,0:00:05.28,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Aurel hated sitting still.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.00,0:00:11.10,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}The painter gave up in the end.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.10,0:00:13.40,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Painted him about to laugh.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.40,0:00:16.90,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}That's how I remember him. About to.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.00,0:00:22.00,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Twelve years a fire-warden in the lower wards.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.00,0:00:25.00,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}You learn to read a fire the way clerks read a ledger.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.00,0:00:29.00,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Where it started. How fast. Who wanted it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.00,0:00:35.20,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Corwen's Wharf burned on a calm night.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.00,0:00:41.00,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}No wind. No lightning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.00,0:00:44.00,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Fires don't start themselves on calm nights.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.00,0:00:47.90,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}This one started in three places at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.00,0:00:52.60,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Aurel was inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.60,0:00:55.10,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Doing the inventory the owner asked him to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.10,0:00:57.30,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}On a Sunday night.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.60,0:01:08.40,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}It was insured for twice what it was worth.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.40,0:01:10.70,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}The magistrate called it an accident.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.70,0:01:12.50,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Took him a week.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.00,0:01:17.50,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}The owner bought a house in the hills that autumn.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.50,0:01:19.10,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}I went to his party once.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.10,0:01:21.20,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}I wasn't invited.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.00,0:01:33.30,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}The Quiet Office found me the week they closed the case.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.30,0:01:35.50,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Officially, we're crown auditors.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.50,0:01:37.80,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Ledgers. Seals. Tariffs.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.80,0:01:41.80,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Unofficially, we read the numbers nobody wants read.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.00,0:01:46.80,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}The lantern is the Office's.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.80,0:01:49.20,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}It shows what magic leaves behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.20,0:01:53.70,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}In this city, magic is something you do quietly, or not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.00,0:02:01.30,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Half this city belongs to the Ahm now.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.30,0:02:03.00,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}The other half owes them.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.00,0:02:05.00,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Their master laughs a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.00,0:02:08.10,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Men who laugh a lot have usually bought the room.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.00,0:02:15.10,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Tyr watches from the hill.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.10,0:02:17.10,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}The city watches everyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.10,0:02:20.10,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Especially anyone with pointed ears.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.00,0:02:25.50,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Brann thinks every case is about money.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.50,0:02:27.20,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}He's usually right.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.20,0:02:29.00,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Pell draws everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.00,0:02:32.00,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Even me, when he thinks I'm not looking.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.00,0:02:38.64,Maren,,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,300)\blur5}Lately the numbers have started leaving bodies.
